{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospitalists. You're here today for your 15th cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your brain lymphoma. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I'm okay, just a little tired. My breathing’s been off this week—I’ve been using my albuterol more often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I saw that in your chart. We’re thinking it might be acute bronchitis, possibly overlapping with your asthma. We’ll manage it with your usual inhalers and add a new one if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I haven’t had a fever or cough, just shortness of breath when I walk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That fits. We’ll monitor it. Now, about the chemotherapy—we’ll give you the methotrexate infusion today. We’ll also start IV fluids with sodium acetate to help protect your kidneys and make sure the drug clears properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember from last time. No bicarbonate IV, right? Because of the shortage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re using sodium acetate instead, and you’ll also take oral bicarbonate pills to keep your urine alkaline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:23:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And leucovorin starts tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 24 hours after the chemo starts. We’ll also check your methotrexate levels every day to make sure it’s clearing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:25:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been nauseated before, but the anti-nausea meds help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given you pre-meds for nausea, and you can have more if needed. We’ll also watch your labs closely—especially liver enzymes, which sometimes go up with each cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:27:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, the transaminitis. It always comes back a little, but it settles."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:28:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and it’s been mild so far. We’ll keep an eye on it. One thing—we’ve held your aspirin during this admission to help the methotrexate clear faster."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:29:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right. Because of the blood clot history. When do I restart it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:30:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll restart it when you go home. You should take it daily again, but stop it two days before your next chemo admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:31:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll mark that on my calendar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, your mesalamine for ulcerative colitis is on hold while you’re here to avoid interactions. If your symptoms flare up at home, you can restart it—just not during chemo stays."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:34:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "After the clindamycin last time, I had bleeding. I was scared. But it’s been quiet since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:35:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that was likely antibiotic-related colitis. We’ll avoid unnecessary antibiotics this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:36:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. My foot pain is still there—burning, up the leg. Not worse, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on gabapentin for that. Tests were negative before, so we’ll continue managing the symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:39:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just wish we knew what was causing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-01-26 10:40:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll keep looking if anything changes. For now, we focus on what we can manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your first methotrexate level came back—it’s where we expect it. No signs of toxicity."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I did feel a little nauseated yesterday, but the prochlorperazine helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve added ondansetron to your discharge meds in case you need stronger anti-nausea coverage at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great, thank you. How’s my breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started you on albuterol-ipratropium, the Combivent inhaler. It helps open airways more than albuterol alone. You should feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve used it twice today. Easier to catch my breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll send that home with you. Also, your potassium and phosphorus were low yesterday, so we’ve been replacing them through your IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, that explains the muscle cramps. Feels better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-01-27 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, those electrolyte imbalances can happen with the fluids and chemo. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You’re doing well. Your latest methotrexate level is down to 0.18, which means it’s clearing nicely. We’ll check one more tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:46:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Any word on the MRI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:47:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The report just came in. The good news is your lymphoma looks stable—no new lesions or abnormal enhancement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:48:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, thank goodness. What about the sinus thing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There’s still some sinus inflammation—mucosal thickening in a few sinuses. But it’s not worse, and since you don’t have symptoms, we won’t treat it now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:51:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Last time I got clindamycin, it messed up my gut. I’d rather avoid antibiotics if I can."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:52:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Agreed. We’ll hold off unless you develop symptoms like congestion or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:53:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my mood? I’ve been sad, but not depressed. I don’t want another psych admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I spoke with Social Work. You’re continuing citalopram, which is important. We won’t push a psych consult unless you change your mind."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-01-28 08:56:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just need support, not another hospital stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your final methotrexate level is 0.13—excellent clearance. Your labs are stable, and you’re breathing better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you. Restart your aspirin tomorrow. Stop it two days before your next chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the new inhaler?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the Combivent as needed for shortness of breath. It’s for possible bronchitis. Keep using your regular asthma inhalers too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the MRI results?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call Dr. ___’s office in a few days to get the detailed results. But the key point is your lymphoma is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-01-29 07:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you for your next cycle."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-01-26 09:59:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-01-29 10:33:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, ulcerative colitis, asthma, and a history of DVT/PE was admitted for her 15th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the treatment well with only mild nausea, managed with anti-emetics. Methotrexate cleared appropriately with no renal or hepatic toxicity. An MRI showed stable lymphoma without new lesions. Her dyspnea was attributed to acute bronchitis, and she improved with a new albuterol-ipratropium inhaler. Aspirin was held during admission to enhance methotrexate excretion and was restarted at discharge. She remained stable emotionally, denying depression or suicidal ideation, and was discharged home in good condition with follow-up instructions.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Ulcerative colitis, unspecified",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Acute bronchitis",
      "Disorders of phosphorus metabolism",
      "Antineoplastic chemotherapy induced anemia",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Nonspecific elevation of levels of transaminase or lactic acid dehydrogenase [LDH]",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Other chronic pain"
    ]
  }
}
